      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I like browsing new worlds. They tend to have between zero and ten users in them. When browsing worlds, you see how many people are currently in a world. This is useful because I prefer joining instances with people. Unfortunately, the player number includes people in private instances. Most new worlds *only* have private instances. This is annoying because I end up clicking on a world thinking that it has players, only to see that I can't join any instances because they are private. Then I go back to the world menu and click on the next world and it happens again and so on. The player count for private instances is useless.\n\nIt would be better if the player count was for public instances only. Or if there was a setting to change this. Or if there were separate private and public player counts. This way I would immediately see which worlds I should join.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
